    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>The great southern kingdom of ancient <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#china">China</a>, based on the middle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#yangtze-river">Yangtze</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#han-river">Han River</a>.</li><li>Its rulers called themselves kings from 704 BCE and absorbed dozens of states, organising many as counties.</li><li>Its distinctive culture produced the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#song-dynasty">Songs</a> of Chu, and Chu rebels overthrew the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#qin-dynasty">Qin dynasty</a> that had conquered it.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The oldest known <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#manuscript">manuscript</a> of parts of the Daodejing was found in a Chu tomb at Guodian, written on bamboo slips around 300 BCE.</p></aside>
    </section>

